138	                deepCut={
139	                  <p>
140	                    The speed was real, and so was the ceiling: the model saw
141	                    one file, one selection. Cursor had to fork VS Code to raise
142	                    it — the extension API allows a sidebar, not an editor that
143	                    thinks; indexing a codebase and editing across files needs
144	                    the core. That&apos;s why Copilot rode along as a plugin
145	                    while Cursor rebuilt the vehicle. The ceiling finally
146	                    cracked late in 2024, when models learned to reason —
147	                    multi-step thinking, the ingredient agents were waiting for.
148	                  </p>
149	                }
150	                expandLabel="Did you know? You were the bus."
151	                name="Extraction → Integration"
152	                reality="It answers now — in a browser tab, a world away from your code. You ferry context in and answers out by hand, until the chat moves into the editor and your selection becomes its context. Either way the verdict held: a senior engineer was faster. The model missed the file next door and the framework's basics, and correcting it cost more than writing it."
